# JUranometria's Norwegian Bokmal interface (Sprint 33, issue #350).
#
# Registering this language is what makes it selectable. Nothing
# lists the interface languages: the build walks this directory and
# writes the index runtime reads, so a language arrives by being
# installed - the same contract the chart language packs keep.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# status=draft, and what that means
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The strings in nb-NO.properties are ORIGINAL TRANSLATIONS written
# for this application. They are not taken from a source, so unlike
# the constellation names next door they carry no citation and cannot
# be corroborated against one: their accuracy is a matter of judgement
# about Norwegian, and that judgement is the owner's.
#
# This says draft until a person who reads Norwegian has said these
# are the words an atlas should use. The study reads status from here
# rather than from a banner in Java, so nothing can call itself
# reviewed by deleting a note.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Incomplete on purpose
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The strings file covers the Settings surface and nothing else. Every
# other key falls back to English, visibly and by the gate's rule, so
# a half-translated interface is a legitimate state rather than a
# broken one - and no key ever reaches a reader as itself.
#
# Making it complete is the rest of #350. Proving the mechanism on one
# surface first is what this is.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Not a chart language
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# This governs the words on the controls. What the sky is called is a
# separate setting a reader chooses separately, and lives under
# resources/sky-language. Registering Norwegian here does, however,
# make "Follow interface" mean something it could not mean before:
# a reader whose chart language follows their interface now gets
# Norwegian constellation names by choosing a Norwegian interface.

interface-schema=1
tag=nb-NO
display-name=Norsk bokmål
strings=nb-NO.properties
status=draft
